  {
    "id" : "AvoidInlineConditionals",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Inline Conditionals",
    "description" : "This rule detects the use of inline conditional expressions (ternary operators) in code.",
    "explanation" : "<div>\n\nDetects inline conditionals. Here is one example of an inline\nconditional:\n\n</div>\n\n    String a = getParameter(\"a\");\n    String b = (a==null || a.length()<1) ? null : a.substring(1);\n            \n\nRationale: Some developers find inline conditionals hard to read, so\ntheir employer's coding standards forbid them.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "AvoidNestedBlocks",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Nested Blocks",
    "description" : "Detects and discourages the use of unnecessary nested blocks in code.",
    "explanation" : "<div>\n\nFinds nested blocks (blocks that are used freely in the code).\n\n</div>\n\nRationale: Nested blocks are often leftovers from the debugging process,\nthey confuse the reader.\n\nFor example, this check finds the obsolete braces in\n\n    public void guessTheOutput()\n    {\n      int whichIsWhich = 0;\n      {\n        whichIsWhich = 2;\n      }\n      System.out.println(\"value = \" + whichIsWhich);\n    }\n            \n\nand debugging / refactoring leftovers such as\n\n    // if (conditionThatIsNotUsedAnyLonger)\n    {\n      System.out.println(\"unconditional\");\n    }\n            \n\nA case in a switch statement does not implicitly form a block. Thus, to\nbe able to introduce local variables that have case scope it is\nnecessary to open a nested block. This is supported, set the\nallowInSwitchCase property to true and include all statements of the\ncase in the block.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "allowInSwitchCase",
        "default" : "false",
        "description" : "Allow nested blocks if they are the only child of a switch case."
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
