  {
    "id" : "BooleanExpressionComplexity",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "Complexity",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Restrict Boolean Expression Complexity",
    "description" : "This rule restricts the number of boolean operators (&&, ||, &, |, ^) in a boolean expression to reduce complexity.",
    "explanation" : "<div>\n\nRestricts the number of boolean operators (`&&`, `||`, `&`, `|` and `^`)\nin an expression.\n\n</div>\n\nRationale: Too many conditions leads to code that is difficult to read\nand hence debug and maintain.\n\nNote that the operators `&` and `|` are not only integer bitwise\noperators, they are also the [non-shortcut\nversions](https://docs.oracle.com/javase/specs/jls/se11/html/jls-15.html#jls-15.22.2)\nof the boolean operators `&&` and `||`.\n\nNote that `&`, `|` and `^` are not checked if they are part of\nconstructor or method call because they can be applied to non-boolean\nvariables and Checkstyle does not know types of methods from different\nclasses.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 10,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "max",
        "default" : "3",
        "description" : "Specify the maximum number of boolean operations allowed in one expression."
      },
      {
        "name" : "tokens",
        "default" : "LAND, BAND, LOR, BOR, BXOR",
        "description" : "tokens to check"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "CatchParameterName",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Catch Parameter Name Pattern",
    "description" : "Ensures that names of catch block parameters conform to a specified naming pattern.",
